00:03:13.088 --> 00:03:15.936
And&nbsp;while I'm at it, I gave these things better names.

00:03:15.936 --> 00:03:17.584
I moved the function to the server module.

00:03:17.584 --> 00:03:22.583
And&nbsp;you just mark it with this decorator in order&nbsp;to make it callable from the client module.

00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:27.740
Then&nbsp;here instead of calling the function directly, we mark it as a server call.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.120
Here, I just pass the&nbsp;name of the function followed by the parameters.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.585
Okay, now it looks like it can correctly tell&nbsp;that the website is up.

00:03:34.585 --> 00:03:37.966
